== what --rent WOULD do, in order ==
   1. list leases here and pods there; refuse if either is occupied
   1b. ARM A DETACHED DEAD-MAN HERE, before the create: it ends a
      pod named mojolearn-gemm-nvidia-<stamp> after
      4500s even if this process is killed
   2. POST https://rest.runpod.io/v1/pods  ->  a NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 pod named
      mojolearn-gemm-nvidia-<stamp>   [THE BILL STARTS HERE]
   3. wait up to 600s for ssh; time out -> TERMINATE
   4. tools/runpod_guard.sh arm <pod> '<ssh>' 60
      refusal -> TERMINATE, no work, no card
   5. key to the pod on stdin (0600), then read the pod's ps back
   6. git archive eb835021dcd79a59a7e8f78c754a75db3c1fea83 -> the box; compare source sha both ways
   7. bash tools/e1_bootstrap.sh, DETACHED and polled, bounded at
      3000s so the fetch keeps its reserve. PHASE 8 IS NOT
      IN MOJOLEARN_E1_PHASES=9, so NO lanes/*.card is written
      and nothing here is a cross-vendor claim.
      READ THIS BEFORE RENTING: phase 9 builds EVERY tier it compares
      -- fast, deterministic and identical -- because a phase subset
      skips phase 3 and a baseline-less middle tier answers nothing.
      That is 4 bindings x 3 tiers of builds. Thirty builds
      took FIFTY MINUTES on a rented RTX 4090 and about three on the
      M4: build time on a pod is not build time on the Mac, and the
      3000s bound is what stands between that and a lease
      spent entirely compiling. bootstrap_exit=124 in remote/leg.txt
      says so if it fires.
      bindings: build.sh build_gbdt.sh build_estimators.sh build_linalg.sh
      lanes:    <all of them>
      A LANE WHOSE BINDING IS NOT IN THAT SET REPORTS REFUSED, which
      is a result and not a silence -- but it is not a measurement,
      so the two lists have to name the same thing.
   8. fetch the bootstrap directory to
      bench/results/e1/2026-09-06_052420-runpod-nvidia; rewrite its commit.txt
      from the pinned sha; read stability/*.txt back
   9. NO SECOND COLUMN NEEDED. The question is whether ONE box agrees
      with itself, and the box answered it.
  10. reap, verify by asking the API, print the lease remaining

